WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.112
A friendly letter uses an address/date, greeting, coherent body, appropriate closing

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:06.899
and correct audience tone.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.645
Where does a date usually appear in a traditional friendly letter? Answer: Near the

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.057
beginning, before the greeting.

00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:19.506
Write a letter to a relative describing a recent school visit and an interesting

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:19.837
lesson.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.751
Why it works: The date identifies when it was written.
